  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **banter - Spark album**: rare: 3 archived performances [3]\n- **Povo**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **Nubian Lady**: rare: 9 archived performances [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2012-06-30.mk4.flac24** (recommended): audience recording; 10 songs; 100 min [1]\n- **soulive2012-06-30.mk4.flac16**: audience recording; 10 songs; 100 min [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Karl Denson appeared throughout the whole show, supporting the album Spark, a tribute to Melvin Sparks [1]\n- Karl Denson played throughout the entire show, supporting the Spark album, a tribute to Melvin Sparks [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2012-06-30.mk4.flac24**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/FOB [1]. Also: This is the 24-bit version of the recording, labeled mk4 in the filename, and not meant for MP3 streaming or CD burning [1]\n- **soulive2012-06-30.mk4.flac16**: taped by Eric McRoberts; transferred by Eric McRoberts; source: Audience/FOB [2]. Also: This is the 16-bit version of the mk4 recording; a higher-quality 24-bit version also exists [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by www.ga-photos.com: [GA-Photos: Flavor Paper Boil in Cobble Hill, Brooklyn > Soulive w/ Karl Denson @ City Winery, NYC - 6/30/12](http://www.ga-photos.com/2012/07/flavor-paper-boil-in-cobble-hill.html) [4]",
